earning","targetRectangle":{"y":108.8184814453125,"x":110.49221038818359,"width":644.39199999999994,"height":59.22399640083313}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":807.29850683036523,"x":299.34906005859375,"width":213.99573915149176,"height":47.144941121495322}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":807.69150630495301,"x":1217.5947992100851,"width":32.408914302564881,"height":39.848206803441258}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":864.6259909425147,"x":299.34906005859375,"width":42.834800283873278,"height":39.665663812787102}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":864.44344795186055,"x":666.24386034246709,"width":32.408914302564881,"height":39.848206803441258}},{"text":"pasted-image.tiff","targetRectangle":{"y":1028.6756591796875,"x":1778.8485870361328,"width":118.83621215820312,"height":34.581336975097656}},{"text":"Performance– Once the model is trained, its performance is assessed on new, unseen data to gauge how well it predicts the onset of diabetes.","targetRectangle":{"y":560.1029052734375,"x":101.91743469238281,"width":1056.99,"height":72.870208740234375}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":411.65289762978244,"x":301.91743290424347,"width":25.250371653405693,"height":33.717337492470449}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":244.92855834960938,"x":1487.1763916015625,"width":149.57999999999993,"height":25.949999999999989}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":452.70703167781653,"x":569.26857215657992,"width":58.740644859813074,"height":33.056074766355152}},{"text":"Experience– Suppose we have a dataset of individuals with the following columns: ","targetRectangle":{"y":367.44589233398438,"x":101.91743469238281,"width":1108.1099999999994,"height":36}},{"text":"￼: Fasting blood sugar level","targetRectangle":{"y":404.31610107421875,"x":301.91743290424347,"width":344.84937165340568,"height":41.054134048034086}},{"text":"￼: Body Mass Index (￼) ","targetRectangle":{"y":445.37023512225284,"x":301.91743290424347,"width":342.58878411214948,"height":41.054134048034086}},{"text":"￼ [Label]: Diabetes Status (0 for No, 1 for Yes)","targetRectangle":{"y":486.42436917028692,"x":301.91743290424347,"width":553.86689719626179,"height":40.392871321918847}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":330.63644409179688,"x":1487.1763916015625,"width":164.57999999999993,"height":25.589999999999975}},{"text":"© Zahra Shakeri, Dalla Lana School of Public Health, University of Toronto","targetRectangle":{"y":1055.1609382629395,"x":54.743599891662598,"width":495.66000000000008,"height":16.580001831054688}},{"text":"label-tag-with-white-details-and-string.png","targetRectangle":{"y":56.325447082519531,"x":778.1090087890625,"width":115.56040191650391,"height":115.56040191650391}},{"text":"￼","targetRectangle":{"y":1051.2967231273651,"x":17.150898866995703,"width":20.015999999999998,"height":21.496002197265625}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":527.8900146484375,"x":1359.0550537109375,"width":158.26222222222214,"height":24.220000000000027}},{"text":"neural-network.png","targetRectangle":{"y":448.97747802734375,"x":1488.2344970703125,"width":159.82780456542969,"height":152.46101379394531}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":415.984375,"x":1490.9263916015625,"width":142.07999999999993,"height":25.949999999999989}},{"text":"Formal Presentation– We represent our dataset as a collection of pairs:￼, where:","targetRectangle":{"y":756.76263427734375,"x":99.34906005859375,"width":1584.9398260023049,"height":39.665663812787102}},{"text":"￼: is a vector representing the health indicators of the ￼ individual.","targetRectangle":{"y":797.29850683036523,"x":299.34906005859375,"width":1095.6746534540562,"height":57.144941121495322}},{"text":"￼ represents whether the ￼ individual developed diabetes.","targetRectangle":{"y":854.44344795186055,"x":299.34906005859375,"width":821.07371458643797,"height":49.848206803441258}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":493.76